 "brief": "# Build: fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o\n\n## Brett said (verbatim)\n> \n\n## What to build\nContinue build \"Fix conflicts and land Build Plan 1 (skins, one-row tables, backgrounds, asset overrides)\" (fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o) [merge] — Phase 1, model Opus.\nModel switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.\nRules: stay in this one session; no sub-agents; steps ≤ 30 min; read only the files listed; stop at the end of this phase.\nLook: UI code (handwritten or generated) conforms to the hot-swappable asset system: every colour, size, spacing, font, radius and border comes from asset tokens (--fx-* colour/style, --fx-type-* / --fx-dens-* / --fx-size-* scale, --fx-radius-*, --fx-border-w; Kotlin: Axf.colors / Axf.type / Axf.space / Axf.shapes), framework controls instead of raw ones, no var() fallbacks. `node framework/cli/check-theme.mjs` and `check-controls.mjs` must pass (CI fails otherwise); `node framework/cli/scale-adopt.mjs <path>` moves most literals onto the tokens.\nAPI: Everything comes with an API (Brett, Nov 8 2026): anything this build adds or changes that has a UI gets full API control: a deep link that opens it (console_show / console_open target), its state readable, and every action and setting it offers callable without the UI, through the console API (REST), MCP tools (console actions, plugin commands, control@1 for tokens and planner items), the CLI and voice (AmberX), all four the same. A UI-only feature is not done; say in the PR how each one is reached.\nBranch: claude/fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o · PR #532\nSteps in this phase (1 left, ~20 min):\n[x] s1 (~30m) Merge origin/main into the Build Plan 1 branch; resolve the 7 conflicts keeping both tap-to-confirm (#524) and the skins work; rebake app copies of ChromeContext from framework\n[ ] s2 (~20m) Run checks, push, open or update its PR, land through the gate; alert Brett if anything fails and retry\nTick each step: node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs act step fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o <stepId> done — it reaches main at once (builds-live). Link your branch / PR: node framework/cli/builds-live.mjs link fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o --branch <b> --pr <n>.\nWatch live: when you start on a screen, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"…\"` so the live preview follows you.\nScreenshots that are not for approval (checking a screen, live captures, before/after): axf shot <file> --name \"…\" --app … --screen … --group \"<build name>\" (UI Review → Screenshots; ui-review-item@1), never the review queue.\n\n## Pipeline\nThis session was started by the orchestrator's dispatcher on Claude account mossesx-max- for the Opus phase. Tick every step as you finish it (orchestrator.mjs act step fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o <stepId> done). When this phase's steps are done, stop: the dispatcher starts the next phase on the right account. If you must stop early with steps left, say why in a build note (orchestrator.mjs act note fix-conflicts-and-land-build-plan-1-skins-one-row-tables-backgrounds-asset-o \"…\"); the build goes back to Pending for Brett.\n",
